WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.633 --> 00:00:07.666
I'm sure there's a Pokémon Center somewhere around here.

2
00:00:07.733 --> 00:00:09.200
Well, I don't see it.

3
00:00:09.266 --> 00:00:11.566
I wonder if the professor's already there.

4
00:00:12.366 --> 00:00:13.833
Don't worry about a thing, guys.

5
00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:18.033
- From over there.
- Let's take a look.

6
00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:04.233
Somebody!

7
00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:07.500
Please, help me!

8
00:01:07.566 --> 00:01:09.300
Hey, are you okay down there?

9
00:01:10.733 --> 00:01:12.433
Hold on. We'll come down.

10
00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:19.833
My leg, it's stuck.

11
00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:23.466
Okay, grab hold of my hand.

12
00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:27.466
- Okay, pull!
- Okay, pull!

13
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:31.333
I can't hold on much longer.

14
00:01:32.866 --> 00:01:34.366
She's in there good.

15
00:01:34.433 --> 00:01:36.333
It looks like her leg's really stuck.

16
00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:39.666
Clemont, can't you do something about this?

17
00:01:39.733 --> 00:01:40.866
Hmm.

18
00:01:41.466 --> 00:01:42.666
Yes, of course.

19
00:01:42.733 --> 00:01:45.900
I thought we would encounter a situation precisely like this one.

20
00:01:45.966 --> 00:01:47.566
Whatever, just hurry up!

21
00:01:48.033 --> 00:01:50.766
Now, stay still and I'll have you out of there right away.

22
00:01:54.733 --> 00:01:56.300
- Ash, quick!
- Right.

23
00:02:08.533 --> 00:02:09.699
You okay?

24
00:02:09.766 --> 00:02:11.566
Yes, thanks a lot.

25
00:02:12.633 --> 00:02:14.666
But how'd you get your leg stuck like that?

26
00:02:14.733 --> 00:02:18.166
I lost my balance searching for this.

27
00:02:19.733 --> 00:02:21.666
It's a Mega Stone.

28
00:02:21.733 --> 00:02:25.000
Right. The truth is, I've been looking for it everywhere.

29
00:02:25.066 --> 00:02:26.966
I can understand why this happened.

30
00:02:27.033 --> 00:02:29.500
What about Professor Sycamore? We're late.

31
00:02:29.566 --> 00:02:31.166
Let's get to the Pokémon Center.

32
00:02:31.233 --> 00:02:33.700
Yeah. Is there a Pokémon Center around here?

33
00:02:34.766 --> 00:02:38.933
Now, you just leave everything to me. I'll thank you by taking you right there.

34
00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:42.000
Wow, you really mean it? Thanks so much.

35
00:02:42.066 --> 00:02:43.233
Pika, pika.

36
00:02:48.133 --> 00:02:49.466
An ambulance?

37
00:02:56.866 --> 00:02:58.700
I can't believe you're Nurse Joy.

38
00:02:58.766 --> 00:03:00.466
Oh, boy. Neither can I.

39
00:03:00.533 --> 00:03:02.166
Pika!

40
00:03:02.233 --> 00:03:05.000
Oh, I always dress like that when I'm out doing fieldwork.

41
00:03:05.433 --> 00:03:06.433
Hop on in.

42
00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:07.733
Okay.

43
00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:14.566
Nurse Joy is so late.

44
00:03:16.266 --> 00:03:18.533
There she is. It's about time.

45
00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:24.266
We're here. I told you it was okay to leave everything to me.

46
00:03:30.633 --> 00:03:33.700
- Thanks for the lift, Nurse Joy.
- And thanks for your help.

47
00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:37.066
First, we hear about a nutty Nurse Joy

48
00:03:37.133 --> 00:03:39.566
who often leaves her Pokémon Center unguarded,

49
00:03:39.633 --> 00:03:42.800
which gives us the perfect chance to swipe piles of Pokémon.

50
00:03:42.866 --> 00:03:45.866
But who knew the twerps and their Pokémon would be tagging along?

51
00:03:45.933 --> 00:03:48.433
It'll be easy to grab Pikachu for a song.

52
00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:50.233
We're right and they're wrong.

53
00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:51.900
Wobbuffet!

54
00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:57.500
That's great. The professor hasn't arrived yet.

55
00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:01.600
This might be a good time to have a look at your Pokémon.

56
00:04:02.066 --> 00:04:03.466
Please. That would be great.

57
00:04:03.533 --> 00:04:06.233
Okay, then. Please, put your PokéBalls in here.

58
00:04:08.933 --> 00:04:11.466
- Nurse Joy, is something wrong?
- Let me look.

59
00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:13.966
- But it's just--
- Hmm.

60
00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:17.000
Huh?

61
00:04:18.966 --> 00:04:21.066
It appears that there's some sort of barricade

62
00:04:21.133 --> 00:04:22.833
just on the other side of the door.

63
00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:26.533
Well, you see-- Open up, Audino.

64
00:04:26.666 --> 00:04:29.100
Did you do this? Oh, you did, didn't you?

65
00:04:29.166 --> 00:04:30.000
Audino?

66
00:04:30.066 --> 00:04:32.300
Hold on. An Audino's in there?

67
00:04:32.366 --> 00:04:34.900
It's my understanding that in some other regions,

68
00:04:34.966 --> 00:04:38.333
Audino works as Nurse Joy's assistant at the Pokémon Center.

69
00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:40.766
Audino, open up!

70
00:04:40.866 --> 00:04:42.166
Audino!

71
00:04:42.433 --> 00:04:43.566
Huh?

72
00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:49.400
- You...
- Are you two having a fight?

73
00:04:50.033 --> 00:04:53.666
Well, Audino's angry because I didn't say when I was going to come back today.

74
00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:55.333
It can get really upset,

75
00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:58.166
and it's going to stay upset for quite some time.

76
00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:02.133
I'm sorry, but would you mind letting Audino and me speak alone for a moment?

77
00:05:07.533 --> 00:05:09.133
So, what should we do now?

78
00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:10.200
"What should we do?"

79
00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:13.466
Well, I'd really like to help the two of them make up.

80
00:05:13.866 --> 00:05:15.500
Pikachu.

81
00:05:15.966 --> 00:05:17.500
- Hey!
- Huh?

82
00:05:17.566 --> 00:05:20.166
- Can you guys talk to Audino?
- Who are you?

83
00:05:20.233 --> 00:05:21.433
I'm Emilio.

84
00:05:21.866 --> 00:05:25.766
- My name is Ash, and this is Pikachu.
- Pikachu.

85
00:05:25.833 --> 00:05:28.266
- I'm Serena. Hi.
- I'm Clemont.

86
00:05:28.333 --> 00:05:31.400
I'm Bonnie. Hi. And this is Dedenne.

87
00:05:31.466 --> 00:05:33.633
- Dedenne.
- And that's Squishy.

88
00:05:34.866 --> 00:05:36.266
Nice to meet you.

89
00:05:37.566 --> 00:05:40.400
Is there any way you can get those two to make up?

90
00:05:40.666 --> 00:05:43.400
They're really close and they usually get along.

91
00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:46.133
You must know them pretty well then.

92
00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:47.033
Come on.

93
00:05:49.833 --> 00:05:51.266
Audino's in here.

94
00:05:51.333 --> 00:05:53.900
We can get to Audino by climbing through this window.

95
00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:06.433
Come on in.

96
00:06:16.833 --> 00:06:18.800
Come on, Audino. Open up.

97
00:06:18.866 --> 00:06:21.166
Let me in, Audino, please.

98
00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:24.133
I'm really sorry for not contacting you.

99
00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:26.033
Audino.

100
00:06:26.933 --> 00:06:27.766
Audino?

101
00:06:29.733 --> 00:06:30.966
Audino.

102
00:06:31.033 --> 00:06:32.466
Please, don't worry.

103
00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:35.033
These nice people are just worried about you.

104
00:06:35.866 --> 00:06:37.066
Audino.

105
00:06:42.766 --> 00:06:46.066
See, we think it'd be great if you could make up with Nurse Joy.

106
00:06:46.133 --> 00:06:49.700
Everyone who comes to the Pokémon Center really needs the both of you.

107
00:06:57.133 --> 00:06:58.466
Audino.

108
00:07:05.966 --> 00:07:08.766
You gotta hang in there, Makuhita. Phew.

109
00:07:08.833 --> 00:07:10.633
- The Pokémon Center's close.
- Huh?

110
00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:12.000
Just a little farther.

111
00:07:14.666 --> 00:07:17.033
- Huh?
- You gotta help us! Nurse Joy!

112
00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:18.900
We really need your help! Please!

113
00:07:18.966 --> 00:07:20.600
But what can I do?

114
00:07:21.066 --> 00:07:22.200
This is bad.

115
00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:25.700
Why don't you let me have a look?

116
00:07:25.933 --> 00:07:27.466
Hey, wait a minute. You're--

117
00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:30.533
You're Professor Sycamore.

118
00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:33.500
Makuhita. - Hmm.

119
00:07:33.566 --> 00:07:35.333
Yes, we must act immediately.

120
00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:37.733
Makuhita needs help right this instant.

121
00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:39.033
Yes, of course.

122
00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:42.033
Open up, Audino! We have an emergency patient!

123
00:07:42.766 --> 00:07:43.666
Audino?

124
00:07:44.633 --> 00:07:45.600
Audino.

125
00:07:45.666 --> 00:07:47.033
Get everything ready now!

126
00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:49.766
- Audino.
- Professor Sycamore.

127
00:07:49.833 --> 00:07:51.100
Hello, Ash.

128
00:07:51.233 --> 00:07:54.233
This Makuhita's in trouble. Will you help us out?

129
00:07:54.300 --> 00:07:57.233
- Huh? You bet.
- Audino.

130
00:07:57.300 --> 00:07:59.066
Unh. Thanks.

131
00:08:03.066 --> 00:08:06.266
- Audino, go ahead.
- Audino.

132
00:08:07.066 --> 00:08:09.133
Who's that Pokémon?

133
00:08:14.066 --> 00:08:16.000
It's Audino.

134
00:08:16.066 --> 00:08:17.300
Audino.

135
00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:24.733
Makuhita.

136
00:08:25.266 --> 00:08:27.566
Maku...

137
00:08:27.633 --> 00:08:28.833
Audino.

138
00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:33.766
Makuhita.

139
00:08:42.466 --> 00:08:43.733
How's Makuhita doing?

140
00:08:43.799 --> 00:08:45.200
It's still being treated.

141
00:08:45.533 --> 00:08:46.600
How is it going?

142
00:08:46.666 --> 00:08:48.833
We just have to leave them to their work.

143
00:08:49.100 --> 00:08:51.100
There's no need to worry with those two.

144
00:08:58.900 --> 00:09:01.633
- What's this?
- You see, Nurse Joy just found that.

145
00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:03.333
It's a Mega Stone.

146
00:09:04.366 --> 00:09:05.200
Hmm.

147
00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:12.700
Makuhita's much better.

148
00:09:13.733 --> 00:09:14.633
Audino.

149
00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:17.266
- Makuhita!
- Makuhita!

150
00:09:17.333 --> 00:09:19.533
Thank goodness you're well.

151
00:09:19.600 --> 00:09:21.366
- Makuhita.
- Oh, come on, come on.

152
00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:24.466
Nurse Joy and Audino, thank you so much.

153
00:09:24.633 --> 00:09:25.766
Makuhita.

154
00:09:26.233 --> 00:09:27.900
Well, it's the least we could do.

155
00:09:29.233 --> 00:09:30.300
Take good care.

156
00:09:30.766 --> 00:09:31.900
Audino.

157
00:09:34.433 --> 00:09:37.066
Audino, what do you say we straighten things up?

158
00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:38.333
Audino.

159
00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:43.233
I'm so glad that Makuhita's feeling better.

160
00:09:43.400 --> 00:09:45.333
Nurse Joy has a lot of skill.

161
00:09:45.666 --> 00:09:48.966
She and Audino are just marvelous working as a team.

162
00:09:49.433 --> 00:09:51.633
You see? I told you those two really get along.

163
00:09:51.700 --> 00:09:53.966
So, why do they always fight so much?

164
00:09:54.900 --> 00:09:57.566
There must be some sort of explanation why.

165
00:09:57.633 --> 00:10:00.833
Oh, by the way, professor, what do you know about Squishy?

166
00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:02.133
Right, Squishy.

167
00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:04.700
Of course, the situation needs to be looked into.

168
00:10:04.766 --> 00:10:06.966
Would it be possible to see Squishy right now?

169
00:10:07.033 --> 00:10:09.333
Bonnie's been taking very good care of it.

170
00:10:09.400 --> 00:10:10.466
Yeah.

171
00:10:11.266 --> 00:10:12.333
Here we go.

172
00:10:13.033 --> 00:10:15.333
You'll be nice to the professor, right?

173
00:10:16.700 --> 00:10:18.566
Squishy, hello.

174
00:10:20.200 --> 00:10:22.466
- It'll be fine.
- Fascinating.

175
00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:25.066
It is rather squishy, isn't it?

176
00:10:25.133 --> 00:10:27.200
That's why I named it Squishy.

177
00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:33.300
So, professor, what do you think?

178
00:10:33.400 --> 00:10:34.833
Is it a new Pokémon?

179
00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:36.633
Well, I really can't say yet,

180
00:10:36.866 --> 00:10:40.833
but I have been busy trying to find answers since you first contacted me,

181
00:10:41.300 --> 00:10:43.500
talking with several research institutes.

182
00:10:43.966 --> 00:10:46.500
There's no record of anything like Squishy anywhere.

183
00:10:47.533 --> 00:10:51.300
So, until we can have a thorough look at Squishy's DNA structure...

184
00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:54.800
we won't know anything for certain.

185
00:10:55.766 --> 00:10:58.300
Just what are you anyway, Squishy?

186
00:11:01.066 --> 00:11:03.166
I told you I was sorry, didn't I?

187
00:11:03.633 --> 00:11:04.666
Audino.

188
00:11:06.966 --> 00:11:09.500
- My goodness.
- And they're at it again.

189
00:11:09.566 --> 00:11:12.533
Hey! Won't the both of you relax? Please!

190
00:11:13.833 --> 00:11:16.033
When did you two start fighting like this?

191
00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:20.033
Well, it started even before we were sent to this Pokémon Center.

192
00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:29.400
An Audino.

193
00:11:29.466 --> 00:11:30.900
Audino.

194
00:11:31.700 --> 00:11:33.900
Everybody else has a Wigglytuff.

195
00:11:33.966 --> 00:11:36.400
So, why am I the only one with an Audino, huh?

196
00:11:36.466 --> 00:11:39.366
When you focus on something, you have a slight tendency

197
00:11:39.433 --> 00:11:42.400
to forget everything else that's going on around you.

198
00:11:42.466 --> 00:11:43.900
Huh?

199
00:11:43.966 --> 00:11:46.400
So, we've decided it would be best to team you up

200
00:11:46.466 --> 00:11:49.633
with an experienced veteran assistant, this Audino.

201
00:11:49.700 --> 00:11:51.766
Aw. Oh, no.

202
00:11:52.200 --> 00:11:55.033
This Audino has been practicing a long time.

203
00:11:55.100 --> 00:11:58.633
I think you'll agree it's exceptionally experienced and skilled.

204
00:11:58.700 --> 00:12:01.933
I'm sure Audino will be of great assistance to you.

205
00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:03.400
Audino!

206
00:12:05.533 --> 00:12:09.033
You see, I have my own way of thinking and doing my work.

207
00:12:09.333 --> 00:12:12.733
You may have a lot of experience, but it's not going to help me.

208
00:12:12.800 --> 00:12:14.166
Audino.

209
00:12:14.233 --> 00:12:18.700
I guess they both have a very strong sense of responsibility, don't they?

210
00:12:18.766 --> 00:12:22.066
Say, there's something I've been meaning to ask you, Nurse Joy.

211
00:12:22.133 --> 00:12:23.600
Huh?

212
00:12:23.666 --> 00:12:26.500
I believe that you were the one who found this, right?

213
00:12:27.700 --> 00:12:28.666
Why, yes.

214
00:12:31.366 --> 00:12:35.766
Look here. When Audino and I were looking for a better method of treating Pokémon,

215
00:12:36.066 --> 00:12:37.500
I ran across this book.

216
00:12:39.433 --> 00:12:42.100
You don't say. That's the book I wrote on Mega Evolution.

217
00:12:42.166 --> 00:12:44.166
That's right. And reading this very book

218
00:12:44.233 --> 00:12:46.600
is how I learned that Audino could Mega Evolve.

219
00:12:47.333 --> 00:12:49.600
- What?
- Audino can Mega Evolve?

220
00:12:50.066 --> 00:12:52.433
- You wrote about that?
- I did.

221
00:12:52.500 --> 00:12:54.133
That's when I got an idea.

222
00:12:54.366 --> 00:12:58.600
If I could somehow increase Audino's healing powers by using Mega Evolution,

223
00:12:58.666 --> 00:13:00.733
we could use it to treat Pokémon.

224
00:13:01.266 --> 00:13:02.233
Audino.

225
00:13:02.300 --> 00:13:05.200
So, that's why you were looking for a Mega Stone, huh?

226
00:13:05.400 --> 00:13:07.066
- Pika.
- That's right.

227
00:13:09.033 --> 00:13:11.966
Well, maybe you should have talked to Audino about that first.

228
00:13:12.033 --> 00:13:16.066
I wanted to surprise Audino by secretly finding a Mega Stone first,

229
00:13:16.133 --> 00:13:17.733
then presenting it as a gift.

230
00:13:18.333 --> 00:13:20.900
Like giving someone a present at a surprise party.

231
00:13:21.533 --> 00:13:22.600
Audino.

232
00:13:22.666 --> 00:13:24.400
I'm so sorry, Audino.

233
00:13:24.466 --> 00:13:27.200
Good. Glad you've cleared up your misunderstanding.

234
00:13:27.266 --> 00:13:30.766
Also, I happen to have a miniature test synchronizer with me.

235
00:13:31.033 --> 00:13:34.633
Why don't we discover just what kind of Mega Stone you found, okay?

236
00:13:34.700 --> 00:13:37.600
- That would be wonderful.
- Audino.

237
00:13:38.300 --> 00:13:39.566
Hmm.

238
00:13:40.033 --> 00:13:42.766
There are plenty of PokéBalls in that room.

239
00:13:43.366 --> 00:13:46.066
So, let's go and grab every last one of them.

240
00:13:46.133 --> 00:13:49.866
- Sounds to me like secret-weapon time.
- Whatever that is.

241
00:13:49.933 --> 00:13:51.333
Turn this thing up.

242
00:13:51.400 --> 00:13:53.333
Let's see what Mega Stone you have.

243
00:13:53.400 --> 00:13:56.000
- A Mega Stone?
- That's what he said.

244
00:14:20.633 --> 00:14:23.300
There's no doubt about it. It's an Audinite.

245
00:14:23.700 --> 00:14:26.200
- Can it really be true?
- Audino.

246
00:14:28.200 --> 00:14:29.066
Here, Audino.

247
00:14:29.600 --> 00:14:31.066
You should hold on to this.

248
00:14:33.133 --> 00:14:35.300
I'm sure it will come in handy someday.

249
00:14:37.900 --> 00:14:39.300
Audino.

250
00:14:40.866 --> 00:14:42.866
- What's that?
- It came from the garden.

251
00:14:45.833 --> 00:14:46.766
A PokéBall?

252
00:14:52.233 --> 00:14:54.166
What's going on here?!

253
00:14:54.233 --> 00:14:56.400
All the Pokémon! Oh, no!

254
00:14:56.466 --> 00:14:58.233
Enough to last a long time.

255
00:14:58.300 --> 00:15:00.200
It's a towering treasure trove.

256
00:15:00.266 --> 00:15:01.933
You guys again? Oh, no!

257
00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:03.833
You'd better stop it, you bad guys.

258
00:15:03.900 --> 00:15:06.533
Prepare for trouble. You twerps are the creeps.

259
00:15:06.600 --> 00:15:08.833
And make it double, we're in this for keeps.

260
00:15:09.266 --> 00:15:11.333
To protect the world from devastation.

261
00:15:11.400 --> 00:15:14.133
To unite all people within our nation.

262
00:15:14.200 --> 00:15:16.833
To denounce the evils of not getting our share.

263
00:15:17.233 --> 00:15:19.833
Which in this case is everything. Hoarders, beware!

264
00:15:20.633 --> 00:15:22.400
- Jessie.
- And James.

265
00:15:23.066 --> 00:15:25.833
Team Rocket blasts off at the speed of light.

266
00:15:25.933 --> 00:15:28.766
Since we've got your PokéBalls, we've won the fight.

267
00:15:28.833 --> 00:15:30.500
Meowth, that's right!

268
00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:34.333
Who's Team Rocket?

269
00:15:34.400 --> 00:15:36.733
Bad guys who steal people's Pokémon.

270
00:15:36.800 --> 00:15:38.666
So, that means our Pokémon--

271
00:15:38.733 --> 00:15:40.033
Say no more, dope.

272
00:15:40.100 --> 00:15:43.066
We're catching them all, and I've improved my Mega-Mega Meowth,

273
00:15:43.133 --> 00:15:45.766
which is even stronger than Mega Evolution.

274
00:15:45.833 --> 00:15:48.800
Presenting the all-powerful Giga Evolution Giant.

275
00:15:48.866 --> 00:15:51.566
It's called the Giga-Giga Meowth Machine.

276
00:15:52.033 --> 00:15:56.133
At first, we thought we'd just take all the PokéBalls in the Pokémon Center,

277
00:15:56.200 --> 00:16:00.266
but now we've put your Pikachu on our list of goodies to grab, too.

278
00:16:00.700 --> 00:16:04.466
And all of your Mega Evolution chatter has also convinced us

279
00:16:04.533 --> 00:16:06.600
to take that Mega Stone away from you.

280
00:16:06.666 --> 00:16:08.400
A catch that's long overdue.

281
00:16:08.533 --> 00:16:09.366
Meowth?

282
00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:16.833
Giga-Giga Meowth Machine, do your thing.

283
00:16:21.033 --> 00:16:23.233
- All right, Meowth.
- Let's reel the twerp in.

284
00:16:23.300 --> 00:16:24.966
Let the fun begin.

285
00:16:27.166 --> 00:16:28.000
No!

286
00:16:30.833 --> 00:16:32.433
You stop right there!

287
00:16:32.933 --> 00:16:34.266
Audino.

288
00:16:34.333 --> 00:16:36.266
Huh? What's the deal?

289
00:16:36.333 --> 00:16:38.900
Now, look. This is my Pokémon Center.

290
00:16:38.966 --> 00:16:40.666
You won't get away with this.

291
00:16:42.066 --> 00:16:44.400
Pikachu's worth more to us than to twerps.

292
00:16:44.466 --> 00:16:45.866
Hey, you read my mind.

293
00:16:45.933 --> 00:16:48.200
- You ready, Audino?
- Audino.

294
00:16:50.266 --> 00:16:51.166
I knew it.

295
00:16:52.800 --> 00:16:54.533
Here, Nurse Joy, take this.

296
00:16:56.466 --> 00:16:57.300
Huh?

297
00:16:58.100 --> 00:17:01.166
With that, you and Audino can do this together.

298
00:17:01.233 --> 00:17:03.133
Mega Evolution will only occur

299
00:17:03.200 --> 00:17:05.599
when two hearts are bound together into one!

300
00:17:06.099 --> 00:17:08.099
- Audino.
- Audino.

301
00:17:08.666 --> 00:17:11.033
Now that they're together, let's make our move.

302
00:17:11.099 --> 00:17:12.633
You heard that, Meowth. Do it.

303
00:17:12.700 --> 00:17:13.833
It's a giga gala.

304
00:17:14.833 --> 00:17:17.300
- No! Nurse Joy! Audino!
- Pika, pika!

305
00:17:17.366 --> 00:17:18.966
- Look out!
- Get away!

306
00:17:20.333 --> 00:17:21.200
All right.

307
00:17:22.666 --> 00:17:24.133
Audino, Mega Evolve.

308
00:17:37.833 --> 00:17:43.566
Audino!

309
00:17:49.200 --> 00:17:51.133
Oh, my. Audino.

310
00:17:51.200 --> 00:17:53.366
- It Mega Evolved.
- Pika.

311
00:17:53.433 --> 00:17:56.033
- Look at that, wow.
- What a beautiful sight.

312
00:17:56.100 --> 00:17:57.866
Absolutely incredible.

313
00:17:57.933 --> 00:17:59.600
Simply marvelous.

314
00:17:59.966 --> 00:18:02.233
I knew the bond between them was powerful.

315
00:18:05.700 --> 00:18:07.966
I've got a bad feeling about this.

316
00:18:08.033 --> 00:18:11.933
Maybe now would be the perfect time to resort to a hasty retreat.

317
00:18:12.000 --> 00:18:14.733
Maybe? There's no time like the present.

318
00:18:14.800 --> 00:18:17.366
We've got to save Ash and Pikachu, Audino.

319
00:18:17.600 --> 00:18:19.600
- Use Power-Up Punch.
- Audino.

320
00:18:27.366 --> 00:18:28.833
Audino, Double Slap.

321
00:18:30.100 --> 00:18:31.200
Audino!

322
00:18:33.000 --> 00:18:34.933
Way too much muscle for me.

323
00:18:35.800 --> 00:18:37.533
All right, use Take Down.

324
00:18:38.366 --> 00:18:40.533
Audino!

325
00:18:40.600 --> 00:18:42.266
Now Power-Up Punch.

326
00:18:43.166 --> 00:18:44.133
Audino!

327
00:18:45.866 --> 00:18:48.800
That Mega Audino out-giga'd our Giga Machine.

328
00:18:48.866 --> 00:18:52.500
Audino, use the strongest Heal Pulse you can.

329
00:18:54.133 --> 00:19:00.866
Audino!

330
00:19:01.133 --> 00:19:04.266
There's nothing like feeling good to make you feel good.

331
00:19:04.333 --> 00:19:06.366
It sure beats being pummeled.

332
00:19:06.433 --> 00:19:07.633
Yeah.

333
00:19:08.766 --> 00:19:12.700
Wow, you know, perhaps fighting is for dumbbells.

334
00:19:13.166 --> 00:19:15.533
Maybe we should give back the Pokémon we stole.

335
00:19:15.600 --> 00:19:17.200
Wouldn't that be lovely?

336
00:19:17.266 --> 00:19:18.833
Sounds totally groovy.

337
00:19:18.900 --> 00:19:20.433
Like a love movie.

338
00:19:25.866 --> 00:19:26.966
Pika, pika.

339
00:19:27.033 --> 00:19:29.200
All right, use Thunderbolt!

340
00:19:30.300 --> 00:19:34.566
Pikachu!

341
00:19:37.466 --> 00:19:41.366
Blasting off is fun when done as one!

342
00:19:51.600 --> 00:19:53.533
Professor, thanks so much.

343
00:19:53.600 --> 00:19:54.866
And thanks to all of you,

344
00:19:54.933 --> 00:19:58.200
Audino and I are finally back to being good friends again.

345
00:19:58.466 --> 00:19:59.300
Audino.

346
00:19:59.366 --> 00:20:01.866
Thanks. And please don't fight anymore, okay?

347
00:20:01.933 --> 00:20:02.766
Pikachu.

348
00:20:02.833 --> 00:20:03.966
We promise.

349
00:20:05.066 --> 00:20:08.366
From now on, I'll make sure to communicate before I go out.

350
00:20:08.700 --> 00:20:10.033
Audino.

351
00:20:10.500 --> 00:20:13.266
So, professor, going back to the lab?

352
00:20:13.333 --> 00:20:16.900
Mm. I'm quite anxious to get there as quickly as possible

353
00:20:16.966 --> 00:20:19.200
so I can do further research on Squishy.

354
00:20:19.266 --> 00:20:20.866
Ha, ha. That's great.

355
00:20:21.833 --> 00:20:22.666
Thanks.

356
00:20:22.966 --> 00:20:25.566
Bonnie, please take good care of Squishy, okay?

357
00:20:25.633 --> 00:20:26.633
I will.

358
00:20:27.633 --> 00:20:30.566
We're gonna head out to the Snowbelle City Gym.

359
00:20:30.766 --> 00:20:31.933
Pikachu!

360
00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:33.266
Have a safe trip.

361
00:20:33.433 --> 00:20:34.633
Right.

362
00:20:34.866 --> 00:20:38.500
After helping Nurse Joy and Audino restore their strong bond,

363
00:20:38.566 --> 00:20:41.433
our heroes are off once again to Snowbelle City,

364
00:20:41.500 --> 00:20:44.300
and Ash's eighth Kalos Gym Badge Challenge,

365
00:20:44.600 --> 00:20:46.900
as the journey continues.
